on time.\n\nQuery Rewrite 6:\nThis rule does not apply because there are no out-of-range constants or range boundary folding opportunities.\n\nQuery Rewrite 7: """Move outer query conditions into the WHERE clause of subqueries when these conditions do not affect aggregations or window functions. Conditions in the outer query not involving `GROUP BY` columns of a derived table with aggregation are transformed into the `HAVING` clause of the subquery."""\nThe query can be optimized by applying the most restrictive selection criteria as early as possible in the query execution. This rule suggests moving conditions from the outer query into the WHERE clause of subqueries or the HAVING clause of derived tables.\n\nNote that these rewrite rules are not mutually exclusive, and some may apply simultaneously to optimize the given SQL query.', 'time': 13.974474430084229}
